#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: Montana
#> pause: 40
#> must: Alabama|
#> must: Kansas|
#> must: # command:  sed  -f
#> not: Iowa  |
#> not: Alabama   |
#> not: ERROR parsing
#> source: s/^[ \t]*//
# 6. Trim leading and trailing whitespace. Pement: sed 's/^[ \t]*//;s/[ \t]*$//'
# Two substitutions: ^[ \t]* is any run of spaces or tabs at the start of the
# line, [ \t]*$ the same at the end; both are replaced by nothing. GNU sed
# understands \t; older seds need a real tab inside the brackets. The third
# command marks the new line end with | so you can see the trailing run went.
# Try: delete the third command and the ends are invisible again.
s/^[ \t]*//;s/[ \t]*$//
s/$/|/

#DATA
   Alabama   
	Alaska
  Iowa  
Kansas	
    Montana
